\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Model rules and a recorded encounter. (a) Dolphins repeat a near-prey herding period, one strike and recovery; birds affect dolphins through fish dynamics. (b,c) Recorded top and side views at 12T for development school 2 with exposed targeting and gannets. Paths cover 6--12T; crosses mark three actual captures. Coordinates are relative to the surviving prey centroid; z=0 is the surface. The snapshot illustrates behaviour, not verified whole-school containment.\relax }}{2}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Development comparisons. Bars show dolphin captures in matched 36T encounters with 12 dolphins alone or with three gannets. Each target rule was tested on two development schools using one set of random draws. Nearest targeting produced totals of 55 alone and 53 with birds; exposed targeting produced 41 and 48. The initial response to adding gannets led us to select exposed targeting for follow-up. Individual outcomes are shown without confidence intervals.\relax }}{3}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Partner effects on the same eight schools. Points show mixed-minus-alone captures; lines join each school across coarse (0.00125T) and fine (0.000625T) grids at 36T. Diamonds show equal-school means. Only coarse 36T primary estimates have 97.5\% marginal bootstrap intervals (approximate 95\% familywise coverage, with small-sample limitations). Fine 36T and coarse 72T outcomes are descriptive checks, not additional independent schools. Earlier cohorts are excluded.\relax }}{4}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Earlier two-school controls and initial-depth pilot, kept separate from the eight-school replication. Matching gannet-only controls and initial-depth results. (a) Changes in dolphin and gannet captures when hunting together; S1 and S2 identify the two fresh schools, and 1 and 2 identify random settings 61001 and 61002. Both species gain in two of four repetitions. (b) Gannet-only captures across initial mean depths, using setting 61001; lines join the same school. (c) The fraction of surviving fish within the reference depth envelope changes during each encounter. Colour identifies initial depth; solid and dashed curves identify schools 1 and 2. Initial depth is not maintained, and the connecting lines in (b) are not fitted response curves.\relax }}{5}{figure.4}\protected@file@percent }
